            "text": "{\n  \"proposals\": [],\n  \"observations\": [\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"(B) Defined benefit plan The administrator of a defined benefit plan (other than a one-participant retirement plan described in section 1021(i)(8)(B) of this title) shall furnish a pension benefit statement—\\n\\n(i) at least once every 3 years to each participant with a nonforfeitable accrued benefit and who is employed by the employer maintaining the plan at the time the statement is to be furnished, and\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The requirement for defined benefit plan administrators to furnish statements at least once every three years is already completely and faithfully represented in C0003, with all statutory conditions and exceptions preserved.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"already_represented\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"(ii) Model disclosure Not later than 1 year after December 20, 2019, the Secretary shall issue a model lifetime income disclosure, written in a manner so as to be understood by the average plan participant, which—\\n\\n(I) explains that the lifetime income stream equivalent is only provided as an illustration;\\n\\n(II) explains that the actual payments under the lifetime income stream described in clause (i)(III) which may be purchased with the total benefits accrued will depend on numerous factors and may vary substantially from the lifetime income stream equivalent in the disclosures;\\n\\n(III) explains the assumptions upon which the lifetime income stream equivalent was determined; and\\n\\n(IV) provides such other similar explanations as the Secretary considers appropriate.\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The Secretary's duty to issue a model lifetime income disclosure within one year after December 20, 2019, incorporating items (I) through (IV), is already fully and faithfully represented in C0021.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"already_represented\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"In the case of a defined benefit plan, the requirements of paragraph (1)(B)(i) shall be treated as met with respect to a participant if at least once each year the administrator provides to the participant notice of the availability of the pension benefit statement and the ways in which the participant may obtain such statement.\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The alternative notice compliance rule for defined benefit plans under paragraph (3)(A) is already fully and faithfully represented in C0027 without omission of governing conditions.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"already_represented\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
